This probing approach offers a simple and efficient way to assess whether certain labeled concepts are linearly recoverable from the latent space. However, it relies on several assumptions, including that labeled attributes correspond to isolated latent directions. Probe loss differences do not necessarily reflect alignment quality, interpretability, or general usefulness of the representations.

