\subsection{Cross-modal attribution limitations}

Figure~\ref{fig:detailed_spatial_queries} shows a case where SPARC's spatial attribution produces less meaningful localization compared to Figure~\ref{fig:same_image_different_captions}. Using detailed spatial queries ("Cat's Ears", "Cat's Eyes", "Cat's Nose", "A Cat"), SPARC generates similar, poorly localized attribution patterns with minimal variation across different text inputs. Although CLIP doesn't match the captions perfectly, it shows more responsiveness to the text input.

