\subsection{Molecules} \label{app:molecules}
\noindent \textbf{Datasets.}
We use the \textit{QM9} dataset with implicit hydrogens. We generate 20,000 molecules for the metrics.

\noindent \textbf{Metrics.}
We use the same metrics as \textit{DeFoG} \cite{qin2025defogdiscreteflowmatching}, that is:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=0.5cm]
    \itemsep0em 
    \item \textbf{Valid:} Fraction of generated samples that can be sanitized using RDKit.
    \item \textbf{Novel:} Fraction of generated samples whose SMILES are not present in the training dataset.
    \item \textbf{Unique:} Fraction of generated samples whose SMILES are unique.
    \item \textbf{FCD:} Fréchet ChemNet Distance \cite{preuer2018frechetchemnetdistancemetric} between the generated samples and test set.
\end{itemize}

\noindent \textbf{Baselines.}

\noindent \textbf{Specific hyperparameters.} We use $\lambda = 0.1$, our Local PPGN layers have a dimension of 128, and the hidden dimension for our MLP is 256.
We do not use perturbed hypergraph expansion.
Our model has 4M parameters.

